  description: Hassium is a chemical element with symbol Hs and atomic number 108,
    named after the German state of Hesse. It is a synthetic element (an element
    that can be created in a laboratory but is not found in nature) and radioactive;
    the most stable known isotope, 269Hs, has a half-life of approximately 9.7 seconds,
    although an unconfirmed metastable state, 277mHs, may have a longer half-life
    of about 130 seconds. More than 100 atoms of hassium have been synthesized to
    date.
